{"name":"Drip","hex":"#a6ccd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"drip","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fall one drop at a time.","To leak slowly."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drop of a liquid.","A falling or letting fall in drops; act of dripping."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drop (liquid)","blocks":[{"text":"A drop or droplet is a small column of liquid, bounded completely or almost completely by free surfaces. A drop may form when liquid accumulates at the end of a tube or other surface boundary, producing a hanging drop called a pendant drop. Drops may also be formed by the condensation of a vapor or by atomization of a larger mass of solid. Water vapor will condense into droplets depending on the temperature. The temperature at which droplets form is called the dew point."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Water_drop_light_art_vijayanrajapuram_01.jpg/330px-Water_drop_light_art_vijayanrajapuram_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drop_(liquid)"},{"title":"Intravenous therapy","blocks":[{"text":"Intravenous therapy is a medical process that administers fluids, medications and nutrients directly into a person's vein. The intravenous route of administration is commonly used for rehydration or to provide nutrients for those who cannot, or will not—due to reduced mental states or otherwise—consume food or water by mouth. It may also be used to administer medications or other medical therapy such as blood products or electrolytes to correct electrolyte imbalances. Attempts at providing intravenous therapy have been recorded as early as the 1400s, but the practice did not become widespread until the 1900s after the development of techniques for safe, effective use."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/ICU_IV_1.jpg/330px-ICU_IV_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intravenous_therapy"},{"title":"Drip (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Drip is the first studio album by South Korean girl group Babymonster. It was released by YG Entertainment on November 1, 2024. The album contains 9 songs, including the title tracks \"Drip\" and \"Clik Clak\", and the pre-release single \"Forever\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Babymonster_-_Drip.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drip_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Water_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Water_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A water drop falling from a tap","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_drop_animation_enhanced_small.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif/120px-Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif/120px-Bouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Drop of water bouncing on a water surface subject to vibrations","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABouncing_droplets_compact_size.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Drop_held_by_surface_tension.jpg/500px-Dro